#: simcontrols.js:73
msgid ""
"Copper carbonate decomposes at about 290&deg;C</br>giving off carbon dioxide "
"and leaving copper (II) oxide."
msgstr ""
"Copper carbonate decomposes at about 290&deg;C</br>giving off carbon dioxide "
"and leaving copper (II) oxide."

#: simcontrols.js:73
msgid ""
"When heated to 80&deg;C-100&deg;C, FeSO<sub>4</sub>. 7H<sub>2</sub>O lose "
"the water molecules to form</br>white coloured anhydrous FeSO<sub>4</sub>. "
"On strongly heating, the anhydrous FeSO<sub>4</sub></br>decomposes to form a "
"reddish-brown residue of Fe<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> and SO<sub>2</sub> and</"
"br>SO<sub>3</sub> gases."
msgstr ""
"When heated to 80&deg;C-100&deg;C, FeSO<sub>4</sub>. 7H<sub>2</sub>O lose "
"the water molecules to form</br>white coloured anhydrous FeSO<sub>4</sub>. "
"On strongly heating, the anhydrous FeSO<sub>4</sub></br>decomposes to form a "
"reddish-brown residue of Fe<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> and SO<sub>2</sub> and</"
"br>SO<sub>3</sub> gases."

#: simcontrols.js:73
msgid ""
"When an electric current is being passed through water, it decomposes</"
"br>into hydrogen gas (H<sub>2</sub>) at the cathode and oxygen gas (O<sub>2</"
"sub>) at the</br>anode. The amount of hydrogen generated is twice that of "
"oxygen."
msgstr ""
"When an electric current is being passed through water, it decomposes</"
"br>into hydrogen gas (H<sub>2</sub>) at the cathode and oxygen gas (O<sub>2</"
"sub>) at the</br>anode. The amount of hydrogen generated is twice that of "
"oxygen."

#: simcontrols.js:73
msgid ""
"When sodium chloride is dissolved in water, it ionizes to form Na<sup>+</"
"sup> ions and Cl<sup>-</sup>.</br>At the anode, Cl<sup>-</sup> ions undergo "
"oxidation to form chlorine gas. At the cathode,</br>water molecules reduced "
"to form hydrogen gas, leaving OH<sup>-</sup> ions. Na<sup>+</sup> ions</"
"br>and OH<sup>-</sup> ions react together to form aqueous NaOH."
msgstr ""
"When sodium chloride is dissolved in water, it ionizes to form Na<sup>+</"
"sup> ions and Cl<sup>-</sup>.</br>At the anode, Cl<sup>-</sup> ions undergo "
"oxidation to form chlorine gas. At the cathode,</br>water molecules reduced "
"to form hydrogen gas, leaving OH<sup>-</sup> ions. Na<sup>+</sup> ions</"
"br>and OH<sup>-</sup> ions react together to form aqueous NaOH."

#: simcontrols.js:73
msgid ""
"Silver chloride undergoes decomposition in the presence</br>of light giving "
"off chlorine gas and leaving metallic silver."
msgstr ""
"Silver chloride undergoes decomposition in the presence</br>of light giving "
"off chlorine gas and leaving metallic silver."

#: simcontrols.js:73
msgid ""
"Silver bromide undergoes decomposition in the presence</br>of light giving "
"off bromine gas and leaving metallic silver."
msgstr ""
"Silver bromide undergoes decomposition in the presence</br>of light giving "
"off bromine gas and leaving metallic silver."

